            <ArticleTitle>Coping with myocardial infarction: a model with clinical applications, a literature review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>167-75</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Following a myocardial infarction any residual symptoms are likely to remind the patient of a possible fatal outcome and be detrimental to successful rehabilitation. Negative psychological attitudes need to be identified early. Intervention to improve the mental state should be introduced to restore self-confidence.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
